      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "I'm trying to get decent performance out of a design, and the gap between the slow and fast corner is massive. But I don't really need the full quasi-military range of -40/125 and 4.5/5.5 ; I'm replicating a chip whose original specifications were for 0/70 and 4.75/5.25.\nIs there any plan to characterize additional corners with reduced range, like 0/85 and 4.75/5.25 that would help with timings for devices intended for commercial rather than industrial/military use?",
      "author": {
        "id": "836201562707198022",
        "name": "romaindolbeau",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "Melkhior",
        "color": null,
        "isBot": false,
        "roles": [],
        "avatarUrl": "2026-10_media/1-B2132.png"
      },
